This product includes software developed by third parties:

- src/vtts/teacher/vits/ (attentions.py, commons.py, losses.py, mel_processing.py, models.py,
  modules.py, transforms.py): copied from rhasspy/piper (commit 73c04d8,
  src/python/piper_train/vits/), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022 Michael Hansen, itself based on
  VITS (jaywalnut310/vits, MIT License). See src/vtts/teacher/vits/LICENSE-piper.md.
  monotonic_align.py is a numba re-implementation of the VITS monotonic alignment search.

- runtime/ports/esp32p4/vtts_port_p4.c: the ESP32-P4 PIE multiply-accumulate approach follows
  espressif/esp-nn (Apache License 2.0), src/fully_connected/esp_nn_fully_connected_s8_riscv_pie.c.

Data used during development (not distributed in this repository, except one short sample):

- InfoRe Technology public dataset No.1 (25 hours, Vietnamese read speech), via the Hugging Face
  mirror doof-ferb/infore1_25hours (tagged CC-BY-4.0). tests/fixtures/sample_vi.wav is one
  utterance from this dataset, resampled.
- Teacher warm-start checkpoints from rhasspy/piper-checkpoints (vi_VN vais1000, en_US lessac).
- Vietnamese Wikipedia sentences (CC-BY-SA) as distillation text input only.
- English Wikipedia sentences (CC-BY-SA) as text input for speech synthesis only.
- Speech synthesized with VoxCPM2 (Apache-2.0) from designed voices, as training data for the
  bilingual Vietnamese-English voices (not distributed).

Baselines compared against (run as black boxes, not included): sanoTTS (Ampixa) and Piper
vi_VN-25hours_single.

